  "id": "mate-selection",
  "term": "mate selection",
  "definition": "Mate selection is the process of choosing a mating partner based on cues that may signal reproductive or offspring-survival advantages. In the source material, it is described especially as females assessing potential mates using information such as body size, fitness, dominance, territory, and other cues rather than relying on a single trait alone.",
